The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the code, documentation and measurements
authored here. This file lists everything in the repository that came from
somewhere else and remains under its own terms.

Kept deliberately, because reproducibility depends on it: the calibration
corpus is what selects which experts survive, so a build cannot be checked
against ours without the exact bytes we calibrated on.


build/survey.txt  and  build/survey.txt.sources.json
----------------------------------------------------
The calibration corpus, ~263k tokens interleaved from eight tagged sources.

  Wikipedia text (tags: hr, en, de, ru, sr, zh, fr)
    From the `wikimedia/wikipedia` dataset, per-language configs.
    (c) Wikipedia contributors, licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
    Attribution is to the contributors of each language Wikipedia; the text is
    redistributed unmodified apart from being concatenated and interleaved.
    Because CC BY-SA is share-alike, this file and any corpus derived from it
    remain under CC BY-SA 4.0 -- NOT the MIT licence above.

  Source code (tag: code)
    From the `code-search-net/code_search_net` dataset, config `python`,
    field `whole_func_string`. Function bodies harvested from public GitHub
    repositories, each under its own original open-source licence.
    https://huggingface.co/datasets/code-search-net/code_search_net


build/*.saliency.npz  and  build/hr-code.plan.json
--------------------------------------------------
Expert saliency scores and the resulting prune plan. These are measurements
taken over Kimi K3's weights, so they are derivative of the model.

  Kimi K3, (c) 2026 Moonshot AI. See licenses/LICENSE.Kimi-K3.
  The licence permits derivative works; its conditions on Model-as-a-Service
  operation apply only above thresholds ($20M revenue / 100M MAU) that do not
  apply to this repository.

No model weights are redistributed here. The plan file is a list of integers
naming which experts to keep; applied to Moonshot's published weights it
reproduces our build bit-for-bit, which is verified in build/verify.log.


